##! `std.string` (11): text. A `String` is its UTF-8 bytes, `str` is the
##! type of a text literal, and `char` is a Unicode scalar value; their
##! methods (`len`, `chars`, `split`, `trim`, `find`, `replace`,
##! `to_upper`, ...) are the prelude's, and `String` is reached from here
##! too (`from std.string import String`; `str` and `char` are built-in
##! names). Grapheme iteration, case mapping beyond ASCII, normalisation
##! forms and `Builder` are not here yet.
